{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0756b1face0a85e69053abd93b70edd96b56401c1869f8bd6498593eb7621231","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"ralph-workflow/ralph-workflow@3d9d847f41fe snapshot b4e9678f061e3d05","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_27aa610eeac30c18096d7325c6ae97414041885b7f812020c0927e10814db29c"],"source_ids":["src_554234629ff25ee7ab417a0f748d4709"],"text":"Ralph Workflow is described as a free, open-source AI agent orchestrator for coding work that takes one well-specified task and runs a Ralph loop with the user's chosen coding agent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","updated_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2f4d0597996b6c14f584cf0a60a9697d135fb11371873bfa1b7208c2c6080760","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"ralph-workflow/ralph-workflow@3d9d847f41fe snapshot b4e9678f061e3d05","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2956905b6107d051f8bd706b6a3d1b9a316b76ca785d02297aa7e0b5d9d0f102"],"source_ids":["src_554234629ff25ee7ab417a0f748d4709"],"text":"The README states the tool is not intended for vague prompts or repositories lacking tests or other guardrails, targeting work too large to babysit but too risky to trust blindly.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","updated_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_34ff02e0e76ad65e22f6596286f51db4a60142ead597023033688841c9732259","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"ralph-workflow/ralph-workflow@3d9d847f41fe snapshot b4e9678f061e3d05","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6e7e6971bd3497ac8836572f4e7687478c585c775603f0a1c51e9e676537d7a2","slc_9f21818b480e9691e209d9f603f8be6c2f25b9a61beaf2827cd07fa661bd0686"],"source_ids":["src_8da7d3fe5da75296b1f082770dfafc72"],"text":"Repository development practice: all tests must fit a combined 60-second wall-clock budget enforced by import-time invariants in ralph/verify.py, with non-circumvention rules against splitting suites or raising per-suite timeouts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","updated_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4242f15bcc11fae734b5dffb4d0fd9978645d757a2c8a17851b57de26db5dcc5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"ralph-workflow/ralph-workflow@3d9d847f41fe snapshot b4e9678f061e3d05","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3887c60cc217be6d071d9254634e2c1a6a8f2415fe741237f5e6b264aca0ebeb","slc_9e305f2f4b70aa215ab256ad82be8eebd01dad711dea4d63f102ccfb91ce0658","slc_e43e516b4c0ef4d29a78845523c5e1e6f084cc6ab5b9a3b2117cab3bc00ce0a4","slc_e66e94fd44ce9ff59601ee7aa50837dbfa10db62128dd04a24783b7d3c3e1006"],"source_ids":["src_8da7d3fe5da75296b1f082770dfafc72"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors must run `make verify` from ralph-workflow/ before completion; it must pass in full with no unrelated-failure exemptions, and a red gate is owned by whoever next observes it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","updated_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_57fcee6b3aa34ec3c979336ece4ab6430d7a4cadd061ff251fff4c0a303e401d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"ralph-workflow/ralph-workflow@3d9d847f41fe snapshot b4e9678f061e3d05","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_816615aebb11b77bc7566c4ce9f3648e7ad09a0722cf5b8d25417f6949f5c8f6"],"source_ids":["src_554234629ff25ee7ab417a0f748d4709"],"text":"The Ralph Loop pattern is attributed to Geoffrey Huntley (ghuntley.com/ralph), with Ralph Workflow positioned as an independent reference implementation of that pattern.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","updated_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5f35a275a7f9bdbc9098083e74a7d98e90dafb82dcefafb0b4c315fa7c55c512","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"ralph-workflow/ralph-workflow@3d9d847f41fe snapshot b4e9678f061e3d05","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_786e5251f64b92cf7bea74ae5ab529e115fd2afbbaebb24beeee3d208cbfb4cb","slc_b3fec49188855c4974f7d212d640a0852eed621ad0a744df502fb4d034e5bdfd"],"source_ids":["src_8da7d3fe5da75296b1f082770dfafc72"],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md mandates trunk-based development with all work committed directly to main, forbids branch creation and pull requests, and permits commits only via `ralph --generate-commit`.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","updated_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6138f051cd67c4496c9d03d8afea6610b0056e37bf62c5624c10fd038c6b5999","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"ralph-workflow/ralph-workflow@3d9d847f41fe snapshot b4e9678f061e3d05","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4d52db16eb35a15125e5756473b68cfd640111303fe032890b88431e9c4df826"],"source_ids":["src_554234629ff25ee7ab417a0f748d4709"],"text":"The product ships nine built-in agent backends: Claude Code, Claude Code headless, Codex, OpenCode, Nanocoder, AGY, Pi, Cursor, and Kimi; the user authenticates one locally and the tool uses it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","updated_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","created_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6f8e35ff842d220ab6115e4de8b5768bb5ccbf9218469d423d5dc458e858dc10","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"ralph-workflow/ralph-workflow@3d9d847f41fe snapshot b4e9678f061e3d05","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_af41d1f96999452b5678559a31350be166e0d2b0f4639a889098068e167ea21e","slc_df29cb157e21f313f30bf6b808a7700dda0007a65e0ff8cb4f02538505ae5633"],"source_ids":["src_554234629ff25ee7ab417a0f748d4709"],"text":"A checkout install provides an `rdev` launcher whose `--version` ends in -build, deliberately leaving any globally installed `ralph` command in place; native Windows users are directed to install the published package via pipx or pip.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:35:18Z","updated_by_operation":"op_937ee4827699493082f8c10afe9f636e"}
